WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.772 --> 00:00:17.512
Zann stammered.

2
00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:21.193
His lips were still numb from the scatter beast's attack.

3
00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:22.914
"How did you—?"

4
00:00:23.614 --> 00:00:25.374
"Save your energy, boy."

5
00:00:25.754 --> 00:00:27.215
Wyssa sounded irritated.

6
00:00:27.235 --> 00:00:30.296
"The more you talk, the more you slow us down.

7
00:00:31.256 --> 00:00:32.993
Now, where are the others?"

8
00:00:33.993 --> 00:00:34.734
Perda gasped.

9
00:00:34.754 --> 00:00:37.815
"This is the old woman we spoke with in Wormwood!

10
00:00:38.756 --> 00:00:39.777
She's Wyssa?"

11
00:00:39.797 --> 00:00:42.478
"Yes," Zann said.

12
00:00:43.219 --> 00:00:45.920
The effects of the scatter beast's magic were wearing off.

13
00:00:46.641 --> 00:00:49.622
But being in the vortex still made it hard to think clearly.

14
00:00:49.642 --> 00:00:51.724
"How did you find us?"

15
00:00:52.084 --> 00:00:52.864
he asked Wyssa.

16
00:00:53.505 --> 00:00:55.606
"How did you even know to look for us?"

17
00:00:55.626 --> 00:00:58.888
"I have my ways," Wyssa said.

18
00:00:59.772 --> 00:01:02.474
"Now we need to get you kids back to Magica.

19
00:01:03.294 --> 00:01:04.455
Where are your friends?"

20
00:01:05.756 --> 00:01:06.776
"Back to Magica?"

21
00:01:07.216 --> 00:01:09.098
Zann immediately thought about his parents.

22
00:01:09.878 --> 00:01:11.699
He couldn't go home until he'd found them!

23
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.660
"You can do that?"

24
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.201
Perda sounded relieved.

25
00:01:15.221 --> 00:01:16.662
"You can get us home?"

26
00:01:16.682 --> 00:01:19.304
"Of course," Wyssa snapped.

27
00:01:19.324 --> 00:01:20.944
"But where are the others?

28
00:01:21.445 --> 00:01:23.046
There should be another Red with you.

29
00:01:23.986 --> 00:01:24.787
A girl, yes?

30
00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:26.628
And the young Void?"

31
00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.721
Zann felt his heart sink as he thought about Gliss, Darb, and Zing.

32
00:01:31.741 --> 00:01:34.002
"They're gone," he said.

33
00:01:34.022 --> 00:01:37.083
"We got separated in the vortex earlier.

34
00:01:38.123 --> 00:01:39.543
I don't know where they are now."

35
00:01:39.563 --> 00:01:41.844
"What?" Wyssa snapped.

36
00:01:42.264 --> 00:01:46.065
She yanked at Zann's arm so hard that he cried out in surprise.

37
00:01:46.845 --> 00:01:49.286
He felt his body being sucked through another wormhole.

38
00:01:51.206 --> 00:01:56.968
A moment later he, Wyssa, and Perda were standing on a cliff overlooking a rough sea.

39
00:01:57.984 --> 00:02:03.846
Cold wind whipped around them, and strange gray birds circled overhead, letting out shrill cries.

40
00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:06.568
But Wyssa didn't seem to notice any of that.

41
00:02:07.388 --> 00:02:08.648
She was glaring at Zann.

42
00:02:08.668 --> 00:02:13.010
"Let me make sure I understand this," Wyssa said.

43
00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.492
"You brought your friends into the vortex.

44
00:02:17.172 --> 00:02:19.313
Then you lost track of two of them?"

45
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:22.594
"Three, actually," Zann admitted.

46
00:02:22.614 --> 00:02:25.475
"Zing, my pet dragon, was with them too."

47
00:02:25.495 --> 00:02:28.096
"You found us," Perda said.

48
00:02:28.116 --> 00:02:29.677
"Can't you find them too?"

49
00:02:30.637 --> 00:02:31.617
Wyssa glanced at her.

50
00:02:31.637 --> 00:02:33.958
"It's not that easy, girl."

51
00:02:33.978 --> 00:02:35.998
"Perda," Perda said.

52
00:02:36.018 --> 00:02:37.479
"My name is Perda.

53
00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:38.879
Not 'girl.'"

54
00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.620
Wyssa gnashed her teeth, and Zann cringed.

55
00:02:43.821 --> 00:02:46.101
He didn't want Wyssa and Perda to start arguing.

56
00:02:46.902 --> 00:02:48.402
Not when his friends were still missing.

57
00:02:48.422 --> 00:02:50.743
"How did you find us?"

58
00:02:51.043 --> 00:02:51.823
he asked Wyssa.

59
00:02:51.843 --> 00:02:54.944
"Maybe you can find Darb and Gliss the same way."

60
00:02:55.832 --> 00:02:58.274
"As I said, it's not that easy."

61
00:02:59.035 --> 00:03:01.938
Wyssa paced back and forth along the cliff's edge.

62
00:03:01.958 --> 00:03:06.702
"The Interworld Tracking spell I used to find you is complicated.

63
00:03:07.362 --> 00:03:12.147
To do it, you need an object that has some of the lost person's magic energy."

64
00:03:13.288 --> 00:03:14.509
Perda folded her arms.

65
00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:17.011
"I've never heard of a spell like that."

66
00:03:17.031 --> 00:03:22.536
"There are whole worlds out there you've never heard of, girl," Wyssa told her.

67
00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.601
"That doesn't mean they don't exist."

68
00:03:27.042 --> 00:03:29.042
"So you tracked our magic energy?"

69
00:03:29.383 --> 00:03:30.003
Zann asked.

70
00:03:30.023 --> 00:03:31.223
"Mine and Perda's?

71
00:03:31.663 --> 00:03:34.905
How?" "Not hers—just yours."

72
00:03:35.805 --> 00:03:36.946
Wyssa stopped pacing.

73
00:03:36.966 --> 00:03:38.306
"I used this."

74
00:03:39.307 --> 00:03:43.148
She reached into the folds of her cloak and pulled out a small object.

75
00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:45.589
Zann recognized it right away.

76
00:03:45.609 --> 00:03:50.431
"That's a chew toy I created for Zing yesterday," he said.

77
00:03:50.451 --> 00:03:51.992
"How did you get that?"

78
00:03:53.172 --> 00:03:54.693
Wyssa tucked the chew toy away.

79
00:03:54.713 --> 00:04:02.677
"Since you created it so recently, it still contains traces of your magic energy," she said, without answering

80
00:04:02.717 --> 00:04:03.438
Zann's question.

81
00:04:03.458 --> 00:04:08.080
"I was able to use it to track you through the vortex and into Fardark."

82
00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:12.223
Zann shivered, but only partly because of the cold wind.

83
00:04:13.483 --> 00:04:18.746
Hearing the name "Fardark" reminded Zann of his visit with Perda to that dark and dreadful world.

84
00:04:18.766 --> 00:04:21.628
"Thanks for saving us," he said.

85
00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.241
"But can't you use that chew toy to track Zing?

86
00:04:25.661 --> 00:04:27.001
He drooled all over it."

87
00:04:27.021 --> 00:04:29.922
"The spell doesn't work that way."

88
00:04:30.322 --> 00:04:31.143
Wyssa frowned.

89
00:04:31.163 --> 00:04:35.864
"It requires magic energy, not dragon drool."

90
00:04:35.884 --> 00:04:39.185
"You said you can get us back to Magica, right?"

91
00:04:39.485 --> 00:04:40.005
Perda said.

92
00:04:40.025 --> 00:04:43.366
"I'm sure we could find something Gliss created there."

93
00:04:43.386 --> 00:04:46.407
"That would take much too long."

94
00:04:46.887 --> 00:04:48.268
Wyssa started pacing again.

95
00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:52.442
"Your friends could be in grave danger, alone in the vortex."

96
00:04:52.462 --> 00:04:55.024
"Then what are we going to do?"

97
00:04:55.304 --> 00:04:55.925
Perda cried.

98
00:04:55.945 --> 00:04:58.547
"We have to find our friends!"

99
00:04:59.867 --> 00:05:01.088
Zann could only nod.

100
00:05:01.609 --> 00:05:03.290
His throat was too dry to speak.

101
00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:07.292
He couldn't believe he'd accidentally led his friends into danger again.

102
00:05:08.193 --> 00:05:11.135
If they were lost in the vortex forever, it was his fault!

103
00:05:12.256 --> 00:05:14.798
Wyssa stopped pacing and looked down at the ground.

104
00:05:15.218 --> 00:05:16.679
She appeared to be deep in thought.

105
00:05:17.559 --> 00:05:19.264
A minute later she looked up.

106
00:05:19.284 --> 00:05:21.185
"I have an idea.

107
00:05:21.805 --> 00:05:26.086
Come." She grabbed Zann and Perda and yanked them through the wormhole.

108
00:05:27.886 --> 00:05:30.847
Soon all three of them were rushing through the vortex again.

109
00:05:30.867 --> 00:05:32.728
"What's your plan?"

110
00:05:33.128 --> 00:05:33.668
Zann asked.

111
00:05:33.688 --> 00:05:40.310
"I know how to make a potion that will show me which wormholes have been used recently," Wyssa

112
00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:46.231
replied. "If your friends managed to get through one and into another world, I might be able to

113
00:05:46.271 --> 00:05:46.812
track them."

114
00:05:47.672 --> 00:05:48.832
"Great," Perda said.

115
00:05:48.852 --> 00:05:51.553
"But what if they haven't gone through a wormhole?"

116
00:05:52.713 --> 00:05:55.174
"Yeah, what if they're still in the vortex?"

117
00:05:55.514 --> 00:05:56.094
Zann added.

118
00:05:56.114 --> 00:05:59.655
"It's not easy to grab one of those wormholes, you know."

119
00:06:00.736 --> 00:06:01.556
Wyssa shrugged.

120
00:06:01.576 --> 00:06:06.037
"Let's just hope they have gotten out by now," she said.

121
00:06:06.997 --> 00:06:09.498
Zann gulped, afraid to ask what she meant.

122
00:06:10.318 --> 00:06:12.339
Still, he was glad that she had a plan.

123
00:06:13.219 --> 00:06:16.040
First they needed to find Darb, Gliss, and Zing.

124
00:06:16.848 --> 00:06:22.033
Then Zann needed to figure out a way to keep searching for his parents—without dragging his friends into

125
00:06:22.093 --> 00:06:22.673
more danger.

126
00:06:22.693 --> 00:06:25.015
"Hold on," Wyssa said.

127
00:06:25.035 --> 00:06:31.841
"I need to find a world that contains the ingredients for my—" Zann gasped, not hearing any more

128
00:06:31.861 --> 00:06:32.721
of what she was saying.

129
00:06:33.522 --> 00:06:39.767
As he slid past another wormhole, an image of his parents' terrified faces flashed through his mind.

130
00:06:40.648 --> 00:06:44.932
The vision was just like the horrible nightmares he'd been having about his mother and father.

131
00:06:45.737 --> 00:06:48.370
Only this time Zann was wide awake!
